# rdna_loci.bed: rDNA regions on the combined human + mouse reference (GRCh38 + GRCm39, Ensembl 113; contigs prefixed HUMAN_ / MOUSE_).
# Reads overlapping these loci are treated as rRNA and excluded from the species-barcode accuracy metric. GRCh38 carries rDNA copies
# and GRCm39 largely does not, so on the combined genome the aligner places rRNA reads on the human copies regardless of species.
# Built empirically: seeded on the human rDNA scaffolds (GL000220.1, KI270733.1), following every locus reads from those scaffolds
# multimap to in both species, merged within 1,000 bp, over eight poly(dT) BOBseq libraries.
# Columns: chrom, start, end (SAM POS-based, matching the read coordinates used by star_taxonomy_illumina.py).
